From 6a0d172c9f91463393729ef317ef79e097bb96b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: basalt-ink-experiments <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:29:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] inkling2: the on-card set of the RAM experts follows the
 conversation (BASALT_INK_ADAPT)

With BASALT_INK_ADAPT=1 (one session, a spill) a round before a decode window, every
BASALT_INK_ADAPT_INTERVAL decoded tokens and after every prompt, adds decode's lookups since the
last round to each RAM expert's score, orders the RAM experts by score (the elastic spill's
copy-back and its way back to RAM follow that order), gives the card buffers of the coldest
holders to the hottest experts without one (bounded by BASALT_INK_ADAPT_SWAPS, with a ratio and a
floor against churn) and decays the scores. With BASALT_INK_DECODE_KEEP_MIB a round also tops the
card up with new copies while that much stays free; they go back before a prompt is read.

Every table entry and buffer is written on the session's stream between two windows, the stream
waited for before the next launch; a buffer holds its blob's bytes, so the output does not change.
The card's share of the lookups is counted where each lookup was served.

Off by default; nothing changes without the variable. CPU test: inkling2_ink_test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
